From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: openEuler RISC-V Package Automation <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: use configured install libdir in pkg-config files

GNUInstallDirs selects the target library directory through
CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR, but the generated pkg-config metadata still hard-codes
lib plus the obsolete LIB_SUFFIX variable.  Use the same configured directory
for both installation and consumer linker flags so riscv64 metadata points at
lib64 without relying on a deprecated option.

Patch-Source: openEuler RISC-V package review
Patch-License: Zlib
Upstream-Status: Not Submitted (automated upstream writes are not authorized)
Remove-When: Upstream generates pkg-config libdir from CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR.
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1185 +1185 @@
-set(libdir "\${exec_prefix}/lib${LIB_SUFFIX}")
+set(libdir "\${exec_prefix}/${CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR}")
